# "Whenever a Gate YOU control enters": Gate Colossus sits in Bot1's graveyard (Wrath of God, turn 2). Bot2 playing Talon
# Gates of Madara on turn 4 asks Bot1 nothing (the refusal is placed after the pass that takes the priority a trigger
# would have given), and the Colossus is still in the graveyard at the start of turn 5 - then Bot1's own Talon Gates
# (the positive control) brings the same question and Bot1 accepts.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Sapphire
Mox Emerald
Gate Colossus
Island
Talon Gates of Madara
Plains x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Wrath of God
Talon Gates of Madara
Plains x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Gate Colossus.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Wrath of God.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Talon Gates of Madara.Play
Bot1.Pass
! Bot1.Accept
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Graveyard = Gate Colossus; Black Lotus
Bot1.Hand.Talon Gates of Madara.Play
Bot1.Accept

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Black Lotus
Bot1.Library.Top = Gate Colossus
